MID_SCXX_04_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_001: So, the king of Brigid has the authority to arrange\na match like this?
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_002: My thoughts exactly. What made him decide to do\nthis anyway?
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_003: What matters is not his authority but his skill.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_004: And not only arrange it, but take part personally.\nI am curious how this "friendly" match came about.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_005: 
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_006: I'm just the messenger, OK? All I know is, after living\nhere incognito awhile, he wants a matchup.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_007: His kingdom, it's smack-dab between Fódlan and\nDagda. What you'd call a stepping-stone.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_008: Our countries are buddy-buddy, but things tend to\nswing our way, and we don't want that to change.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_009: You're saying it's a friendly match—except that for\nthe continent's future, we can't lose.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_010: What I'm saying is... Yeah, that. And be smart, OK?
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_011: I was hoping Gaitz would join in, but the hermit\nwanted to sit it out and watch.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_012: Hm...
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_013: Commissioner Poloni's on the hook, so he's rooting\nfor you, whatever that's worth.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_014: Not as much as the gold he'll give me.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_015: Right—you still have to scrape together funds to\nfinish the Trial of the Chariot.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_016: Well, if you do win this thing, the prize oughta be\npretty generous.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_017: If we win this, it'll help my friend. That's all the\nmotivation I need.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_018: I care not about your crimes. The chains will impede\nyou. Remove them.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_019: There are facets to this I had not anticipated. Very\nwell, then. I am not one to shy from a challenge.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_020: 
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_021: You have my thanks. With your help, maybe at\nlong last, I can overcome the Trial.
MID_SCXX_04_01_m01_022: Now, let's go and win this.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_001: Salutations, friends! We are Penrose Peregrinus!\nRuler of the proud kingdom of Brigid!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_002: What? That guy's the king? He's not much older\nthan me.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_003: To seek a fight so young? My interest is piqued.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_004: That's the one from the islands of the spirits. He's\neven younger than I was at my coronation.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_005: 
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_006: We have ourselves planned this fine contest. The\nwinning condition—defeat the most giants!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_007: So, fight hard, warriors! Let this battle be a true\ntest of Dagda's and Brigid's abilities!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m01_008: Hm. He doesn't seem so bad.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_001: Uh-oh. That's bad news for us, right?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_002: Hm. We were beaten to the prize. This exceeds\nmy expectations.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_003: It is shameful for the queen of Saramis to fall behind.\nThis king of Brigid must have hidden reserves.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_004: 
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_005: Hahaha! Has Brigid come out on top already?\nDagdan Empire, we fear you not!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m02_006: We've got our work cut out for us.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m03_001: Your loyalty is moving, Cai. But...do you think you're\ntoo quick to run to others' aid?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m03_002: Sorry. I just don't want to feel like I'm failing\na friend.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m03_003: Alright... You're certainly an unusual boy.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m04_001: White-Maned Demon. I propose a contest. Who can\nhunt the most foes—you or I?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m04_002: I'm not opposed, but are you sure we have the time?\nBrigid is more formidable than I expected.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m05_001: I will not brook a loss here. Remember the offer I\nextended to you after that exhibition match.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m05_002: What you said about my becoming your subject?\nI remember. But let's win this match first.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m06_001: Watching you fight up close will be a learning\nopportunity for me.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m06_002: Fair enough—I'm used to being watched. Just keep\nan eye on them too.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07_001: Ah! Bertrand the hero! Your name reaches far\nand wide.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07_002: You honor me. Though my name isn't of much\nrelevance at present.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07_003: You have it wrong. Your reputation has brought\nus directly to you!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07_004: What a pleasure it is to face you at last!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m07_005: You seem like a good king. Very well. I'll follow your\nlead and try to enjoy myself.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m08_001: Oho! So, you strike at our person! We suppose there's\nno rule against it.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m08_002: You gave me an opening—I took it. As a warrior,\nI had to.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m08_003: Haha! Yes, yes! You are every bit the fine\nfellow we had thought!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m09_001: You're turning your blade against me? I suppose the\nrules allow it.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m09_002: We ourselves have hoped to meet you in battle,\nface to face. You won't back away, will you?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m09_003: Never. Come at me, King of Brigid!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m10_001: Your skill is quite worthy of note! Will you duel?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m11_001: Theodora, was it? We are honored to square with a\nvaliant queen such as you!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m11_002: The honor is mine. Each of us represents a nation—\nwe owe it to our peoples to fight to the fullest.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m12_001: Witness the king of Brigid's full power!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m13_001: Peppe! I...I can't believe it's you! What in the\nworld?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m13_002: Lady Ultand! A radiant vision, as always! And a\nparagon of courage!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m13_003: We would like to chat with you once this battle is\nover. But for now...we hold nothing back!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m14: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m14_001: It seems I'm fated to fight giants. Well, I'll win again,\njust like before.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m15: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m15_001: Penrose Peregrinus. I have to say, I'm charmed by\nhis ebullience.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m15_002: His ebulli... Huh? Whatever you said, the brat's got\nnothing on you!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m16: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m16_001: The White-Maned Demon and the Boy King in a\nfierce contest, toppling titans... Where is my quill?!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m16_002: Can the writing wait, Dante?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m17: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m17_001: Heh heh HEH! Hey, Bertie! Where's our\nbuddy Gaitz?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m17_002: He said he wanted to spectate. I'm sure he had\nhis reasons.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m17_003: Aww, what a shame! Missin' out on all the fun.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m17_004: But that means there's more grist for the\nInfernal Clown!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m18: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m18_001: You thought that would be enough?
MID_SCXX_04_02_m19: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m19_001: Urgh. We mustn't fall in battle here. We would be\ndisrespecting this warrior contest!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m20: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m20_001: This isn't easy, but I'm not giving up.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m21: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m21_001: Aagh! Hehehe... Very good! But now it is my turn!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m22: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m22_001: Most impressive. Yet not enough to fell a queen.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m23: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m23_001: A painful blow... But it isn't enough to make\nme retreat.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m24: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m24_001: Owww! I-I can't fall! I need to talk to Peppe!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m25: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m25_001: Ow! More of a hurtin' than I expected. But I give\nas good as I get!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m26: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m26_001: N-no! I refuse to retreat from such an\ninteresting scene.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m27: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m27_001: Gyah... I ain't leaving the stage! More dancing to do.\nJust need a breather.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_001: We've taken out enough! Victory is secured.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_002: You did it, Bertrand!
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_003: It is ended. It was not the duel I dreamed of, but it\nwill suffice.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_004: Good. Brigid has seen our true strength this day.
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_005: 
MID_SCXX_04_02_m28_006: W-well, we are a gracious loser...and concede\nthe loss.
MID_SCXX_04_e04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e04_001: <DLG>The giant consumed the bait from Bertrand's side.\n\nPieces of bait remaining: {Variable=0}
MID_SCXX_04_e05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e05_001: <DLG>The giant consumed the bait from Bertrand's side.\n\nThere are no more pieces of bait.
MID_SCXX_04_e06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e06_001: <DLG>The bait's effects wore off.
MID_SCXX_04_e07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e07_001: We have, in our generosity, given you {SetColor=Gold}three pieces{SetColor=Default}\nof {SetColor=Gold}giant bait{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SCXX_04_e08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e08_001: <DLG>The giant consumed the bait from Brigid's side.
MID_SCXX_04_e09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e09_001: This bait will be quite amusing! {SetColor=Gold}Throw it at a giant{SetColor=Default},\nand the creature will be {SetColor=Gold}invulnerable{SetColor=Default} for a short time.
MID_SCXX_04_e09_002: For that time, the giant {SetColor=Gold}won't attack the army {SetColor=Default}that\n{SetColor=Gold}fed it the bait{SetColor=Default}. Use it to your advantage!
MID_SCXX_04_e10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e10_001: Ah! Have you already used all of your bait? Then we\nwill provide you more. Make good use of it!
MID_SCXX_04_e11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_04_e11_001: <DLG>You got three pieces of bait.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_001: Good going—you won it! Ya beat Brigid!
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_002: I would say I never doubted you, but I'd be lying.\nRegardless, thank you.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_003: Ha! Don't mention it.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_004: I do not need your thanks. But you may call on\nme again.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_005: Spare me this empty flattery and give Bertrand\nhis due.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_006: 
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_007: I'll see that Bertrand gets his reward. Gabriel will\ndeliver it in time.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_008: Soon, Aswan. Just a little longer before the Trial\nis over...
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_009: Why are you huddling together? Is it to plan a feast?\nThen you MUST invite us!
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_010: Y-Your Majesty Penrose, I'm not sure that's proper.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_011: After all of this, formalities must now bend the\nknee...to friendship.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_012: The display of your abilities here has inspired and\nimpressed us. A reward is forthcoming.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_014: Wow. Thanks. That's very, uh, kingly of you.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_015: Given your skill, I can accept this.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_016: A queen needs no reward. But I shall accept in honor\nof the young king's excellent showing.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_017: 
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_018: It was a truly satisfying match! Still, know that were\nanother contest held, Brigid would reign supreme.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_019: If our countries are to meet in battle again, I hope it\nis in a show of skill like this, not a war.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_020: Yes, that is our wish too. May we continue our\nfriendly relations.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_021: Ahe-hem. As a merchant, I got a few ways in mind\nwe can pull that off.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_022: Is this...trade you speak of? Share your thoughts!\nWe are eager and generous!
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_023: That's what I like to hear! OK, OK, so...
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_024: Gabriel, negotiating with the king? You'd best cut\nme in too.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_025: Hahaha! Another contest, over us? Well, the king of\nBrigid welcomes it!
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_026: Seems like they'll be at it for a while—so they're off\nmy back, at least.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_027: Looks like they're having fun. If that's all settled,\nmaybe we should have a real party.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_028: You will find me at the Heroic Games. I am eager.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_029: Their petty squabbles aside, it was a thrilling match.\nI would relish another chance to fight with you.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_030: 
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_031: Heh. I won't say no to that.
MID_SCXX_04_03_m01_032: I really enjoyed fighting side by side. Hopefully we\ncan do so again someday.